# Decision record: resident projection contract, 0.6.0.
# The statement is the resident collapse; body carries implementation rationale.
"@context": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/context/v1"
"@id": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/decision-resident-working-set"
"@type": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/ontology/Decision"
label: "AGENTS.md is a resident working set, not the situation archive"
references:
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-16-agents-md-register"
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-01-possibility-space"
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/decision-vertex-face-body"
statement: >
  Chose the 0.6.0 resident-projection contract: situation/ is the complete
  canonical store and every YAML-LD source validates, while AGENTS.md carries
  only current operational knowledge. Definition, architecture, current
  risks, and every Decision are resident; only active Plans project a compact
  routing face; draft/done/abandoned Plans, episodic records, references,
  bodies, and active-plan execution payload stay cold behind disclosed paths.
  Resident vertex edges must close over resident vertices or repo paths.
  Rejected: injecting every historical Plan/record — unbounded context noise;
  deleting history to save context — loses the canonical store; per-agent or
  branch-dynamic artifacts — breaks determinism, C1 byte review, and shared
  situatedness; completed-plan tombstones — still scale with history. Revisit
  if active routing faces themselves dominate context, or a cold source class
  becomes current truth often enough to deserve explicit residency.
timestamp: "2026-08-23T18:00:00"
body: |
  ## Two truths with different jobs

  situation/ is storage truth: complete source, history, evidence, and depth.
  AGENTS.md is delivery truth: the bounded graph every agent receives before
  it knows the task. Conflating them made every past execution tax every
  future task. The compiler now validates the former and projects the latter.

  ## Plans are episodic working memory

  A Plan declares disposition.state from birth. Draft stays source-only.
  Active contributes only its routing face: type, label, intent, graph edges,
  synthesized state, and document pointer. The executing agent follows that
  pointer for acceptance criteria, tasks, witnesses, reflection depth,
  residual, statement, and body. Done or abandoned returns entirely to cold
  source. Reflection promotes only durable consequences into definition,
  architecture, current risk, or a Decision.

  ## History remains discoverable

  The resident SituationStructure vertex points at all six namespaces. An
  agent asked to investigate history knows plan/ and record/ exist and can
  search them without receiving an enumeration on unrelated tasks. Cold is a
  delivery decision, never deletion or weaker validation.

  ## Projection integrity

  Full-source C5 resolution runs before projection. C11 then rejects a
  resident vertex IRI edge whose target is cold: an injected edge without an
  injected node is a lie. Historical evidence crosses the boundary through a
  repo-path pointer; durable knowledge crosses by promotion into a resident
  vertex. The compiler never silently rewrites relationship semantics.

  ## Determinism

  Residency derives only from checked-in source type and Plan state. It never
  depends on the current branch, GitHub, the invoking agent, or runtime task.
  The same commit produces the same bytes, C1 remains reviewable in the PR,
  and every agent begins from the same situated working set.
